description:
In repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/feature-compose.ts, report each drafting model's outcome so the model selector finally earns a feature_compose posterior. TWO edits in this one file; both are required and together they are complete.

Edit A. Replace this line, which occurs exactly once:
  console.log("[fc-draft-model] selected=" + String((j as { model_selection?: { selected?: unknown } })?.model_selection?.selected ?? "unknown") + " task=feature_compose");

with:
  const __sel = String((j as { model_selection?: { selected?: unknown } })?.model_selection?.selected ?? "unknown");
  if (__sel !== "unknown") {
    (globalThis as Record<string, unknown>).__fcDraftModel = __sel;
    (globalThis as Record<string, unknown>).__fcDraftEndpoint = endpoint;
  }
  console.log("[fc-draft-model] pick=" + __sel + " task=feature_compose");

Edit B. Replace these two consecutive lines, which occur exactly once:
    writeFileSync(
      reportPath,

with:
    void (async () => {
      try {
        const gm = String((globalThis as Record<string, unknown>).__fcDraftModel ?? "");
        const ge = String((globalThis as Record<string, unknown>).__fcDraftEndpoint ?? "");
        if (!gm || !ge) return;
        const gr = verdict === "FAVORABLE";
        await fetch(ge, {
          method: "POST",
          headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json", Authorization: "ApiKey " + METABOB_API_KEY },
          body: JSON.stringify({ type: "llmArmOutcome_write", model: gm, reached: gr, task_type: "feature_compose" }),
        });
        console.log("[fc-draft-model] graded=" + gm + " reached=" + String(gr));
      } catch { /* grading is best effort */ }
    })();
    writeFileSync(
      (reportPath),

The receiving endpoint ALREADY EXISTS and is verified live: the llm-resolver vessel serves the shape llmArmOutcome_write, landed in commit fec22cbc, and an operator probe returned resolved true with shape llmArmOutcomeWriteResult. Its handler forwards to recordArmOutcome, which already maintains the per-task task_alpha and task_beta posteriors and already grades the seven task types that have them. So nothing here is a stub: edit A records which model drafted and where it came from, edit B reports that model and whether the compose reached, and the existing handler records it.

Why it matters: drafting is currently the ONLY work the selector collects no evidence about - feature_compose and patch_with_tools carry zero learned posterior while seven other task types are graded - so model choice for authoring code rides on reputation earned at unrelated tasks. METABOB_API_KEY is already in scope in this file. The report is fire-and-forget inside a try block and cannot affect any verdict.

